    "Net-(U5--): C10.2, R6.1, R7.1, R8.1, R9.1, R12.1, U5.2; /To OPA549: C10.1, U5.6, J3.3; R9 = 20k, C10 = 0.1µF. Loop unity-gain frequency of the R9 path = 1/(2π·20k·0.1µ) ≈ 80 Hz, coarse path time constant 47k·0.1µ ≈ 4.7 ms. In the full driver (prep/Bias Coil Driver Full002) U5.6 feeds U7 OPA549 +IN directly.",
    "Add a clamp or limit on the U5 output (series resistor plus back-to-back zeners, or a 'loop enable' switch/relay that shorts C10 when the coil driver is disabled), and power the OPA549 board before or with this board. A large resistor across C10 (about 1 to 10 MΩ) would stop creep but adds a small DC error, so decide against the required current accuracy.",
