    "Schematic: R3 = R10 = 50kΩ. Summing Circuit V5.csv: R3 = R10 = 3.9kΩ. DRC [footprint_symbol_mismatch] for R3 and R10 (symbol value 3.9kΩ). With R5/R11 = 100Ω and R8/R12 = 50k to the summing node, gain from AC or DC SIG to the shunt-voltage setpoint (through R9 20k) = 20k·100/(R·100+R·50k+5M): 50k gives about 8.0e-4, 3.9k gives about 1.0e-2. For comparison Fine (R2 = 10k) gives 4.0e-3 and Coarse 0.387.",
